&lt;h3&gt;Essential&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some commercial data science experience — typically 1–2 years, or a strong placement/internship record alongside a quantitative degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;SQL&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to collaborate on shared code and avoid technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep knowledge of a handful of machine learning algorithms&lt;/strong&gt; — not breadth for its own sake, but real understanding of a few methods and when they apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to &lt;strong&gt;systematically debug&lt;/strong&gt; unfamiliar code, using AI tooling to accelerate rather than to guess while still understanding problem fully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong AI fluency&lt;/strong&gt; — you understand how to optimally start a task with AI, you use it to unblock cross-team dependencies, and you always QA the output for accuracy and brevity before it goes anywhere&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident completing work independently once scope is agreed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to communicate with clients and colleagues with only minor assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine attention to detail — much of this work involves noticing when a number is wrong&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS or comparable cloud tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automated QA tooling and test coverage practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any experience with marketing, ecommerce, or advertising data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Bayesian methods, marketing mix modelling, or experimental design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Not required&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; need prior experience with marketing mix modelling, attribution methodology, incrementality testing, or Bayesian modelling. These are taught here, and we&#39;d rather hire someone who learns fast than someone who arrives pre-loaded.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll grow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We run a published Data Science Career Development Framework with six levels. You&#39;d join at Developing, where the expectations are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency &amp;amp; Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Understands how to optimally start all relevant tasks with AI; confident completing work independently; uses AI to push for acceptance criteria and limit cross-department dependencies; always QAs AI output for accuracy and brevity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Machine Learning &amp;amp; Modelling:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep knowledge of a handful of algorithms, and familiarity with the full Fospha model suite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering &amp;amp; Codebase:&lt;/strong&gt; Systematically debugs issues with AI support, even in partly familiar repositories; uses supplied AWS tooling efficiently and understands the data science parts of the pipelines; uses existing QA automation effectively; avoids technical debt and collaborates well on code; reviews AI-assisted code so it ships with minimal bugs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicates with clients and colleagues with minor assistance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Complexity:&lt;/strong&gt; Undertakes moderately difficult tickets while starting to become an internal data science champion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervision:&lt;/strong&gt; Receives detailed instruction, but becomes progressively less dependent on senior colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Progression to &lt;strong&gt;Career&lt;/strong&gt; level is against explicit, published criteria — leading larger production projects, resolving bugs independently, and communicating as a modelling expert in your own right. You&#39;ll know what you&#39;re working towards from your first week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Throughout, we look for the same core behaviours: concise communication, collaboration, problem solving, critical thinking, growth mindset, attention to detail, time management, and initiative.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Fospha&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real methodological depth.&lt;/strong&gt; Bayesian attribution, MMM, geo lift testing, and causal inference are our day job, not a side project. You&#39;ll be working on all of it, not adjacent to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Published career framework.&lt;/strong&gt; No guessing what the next level requires or when you&#39;ll get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A team that reviews each other&#39;s work properly.&lt;/strong&gt; Code review and methodology critique from people who care about getting the model right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct client impact.&lt;/strong&gt; The models you build and maintain drive real budget decisions at brands you&#39;ll recognise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working — across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop — down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, Adanola and Huel use Fospha up to 25 times a day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform — and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha builds the products our customers rely on every day to make multi-million dollar media decisions. You&#39;ll work across the full stack — from frontend UI/UX through to backend services, databases, and APIs in Python — alongside engineers, product managers, and AI agents as part of our AI-first operating model. You&#39;ll have the chance to make real code impact across our technical stack from day one, with senior engineers supporting you as you build ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone with some hands-on software engineering experience (professional, placement, or strong personal/academic projects) who wants to go deeper. You&#39;ll take on interesting but achievable work with a supportive team structure and a company that rewards high agency with ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver small-to-medium features independently — frontend UI in React/Next.js, backend services and APIs in Python, working with databases (Aurora PostgreSQL, DynamoDB) — with decreasing need for step-by-step direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, tested code, and grow your ownership within a system area over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate actively in code reviews and design discussions — giving and receiving candid feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own bug resolution and act on QA feedback, improving test coverage as you go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with AI agents as part of our AI-first operating model, learning to write clear specifications that shape high-quality, AI-assisted engineering work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate proactively with product managers, designers, and fellow engineers to turn requirements into working software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get involved across the full Software Development Lifecycle — planning, execution, release, and production monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start building the habits of ownership: consistent delivery, low rework, and steady, visible skill growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some hands-on software engineering experience — internships, placements, personal/open-source projects, or up to ~2 years professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of React.js or Next.js, a solid foundation in Python, and some exposure to databases (SQL or NoSQL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being reviewed and iterating on feedback quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine attention to detail and a real interest in why something broke, not just that it did&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI-assisted development and a willingness to learn spec-driven ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident asking for help and pushing for clarity rather than staying blocked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to REST/GraphQL APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Git/GitHub and PR-based workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some exposure to AWS or another cloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing or maintaining automated tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TypeScript experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in AI-assisted coding tools (we use Claude Code day-to-day)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any exposure to Data Science / Data Engineering workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A £1,000/year flexible benefits allowance to put towards private medical insurance, dental cover, a health cash plan, gym membership, extra holiday, or a pension top-up — whatever suits you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Wellhub, giving you one membership across gyms, boutique studios, and wellbeing apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days&#39; annual leave plus 8 UK bank holidays, an extra day off for your birthday, and more holiday the longer you stay (26 days after 3 years, 27 after 6)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular socials, free weekly snacks, and Lunch &amp;amp; Learn events at our Scale Space office, plus access to the wider Blenheim Chalcot community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to travel — including to our India and North America offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance worth 4x your annual salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Fospha&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real end-to-end ownership. You&#39;ll ship features that drive real budget decisions at brands you&#39;ll recognise, not just tickets in isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A published career framework. No guessing what the next level requires or when you&#39;ll get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team that reviews each other&#39;s work properly. Code review from people who care about getting it right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-first operating model where lean, high-autonomy teams ship fast and learn faster — with structured mentorship from senior engineers as you build that fluency yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values and Principles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be able to demonstrate examples of our core principles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seek inclusion &amp;amp; diversity:&lt;/strong&gt; We create an environment where everyone feels welcome, and people are encouraged to speak and be heard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Hard, Work Well, Work Together:&lt;/strong&gt; We take responsibility for making things happen, independently and together; we help colleagues in need and close loops, making sure our work is complete and has lasting impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow:&lt;/strong&gt; We are proactive, curious and unafraid of failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer at the heart:&lt;/strong&gt; We care about the customer, feel their pain and love building product that solves their biggest problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candour with caring:&lt;/strong&gt; We deliver candid feedback with kindness and receive it with gratitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fospha is the measurement system enterprise retail and ecommerce brands run their business on. We give marketing teams one clear, daily view of what&#39;s actually working - across every channel and everywhere they sell, from their website to Amazon and TikTok Shop - down to the level of a single ad or piece of creative. It replaces guesswork and gut feel with a number marketing, finance and agencies can all trust and act on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brands including Dyson, Gymshark, Adanola and Huel use Fospha up to 25 times a day to decide where budget should move next. We&#39;ve spent over a decade building this, with more than $40 billion in marketing spend now optimised through the platform - and we&#39;re scaling fast across London, Mumbai and Austin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Fospha is pioneering the future of marketing intelligence, moving enterprise retailers beyond the broken world of click-based attribution. Our mission is to transform complex data into the single, most trusted source of truth for CMOs and CFOs managing high-stakes budgets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Marketing Science, your focus will be acting as the technical authority for our Enterprise tier, serving as a dedicated conduit between our Customers, Customer Teams, Data Science, and Product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a rigorous, analytical practitioner ready to operationalize advanced modelling into tangible business decisions, driving sustainable growth for clients like Huel, Dyson, and Gymshark. You will operate as a post-sales, value-delivery engine embedded directly within the Customer Success department. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client-Facing Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively and reactively support Customer Success and Account Management teams on model trust and methodology escalations, directly combating objections related to competitors like Triple Whale or Northbeam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incrementality &amp;amp; Learning Agendas:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary Marketing Science Strategist, designing first-party incrementality tests, calibrating models, and building structured learning agendas for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;R&amp;amp;D &quot;Mouthpiece&quot;:&lt;/strong&gt; Systematically capture and triage field feedback and methodological objections, feeding structured intelligence back to our Product and Data Science teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collateral &amp;amp; Knowledge Creation:&lt;/strong&gt; Build the definitive technical collateral, Academy content, and internal training to raise the baseline data literacy of our entire Go-To-Market organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are we looking for?&lt;/strong&gt; We hire for potential - you should apply if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Science Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 3-5 years of experience in marketing science, data analytics, or technical account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement &amp;amp; AdTech Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of Media Mix Modeling (MMM), Multi-Touch Attribution (MTA), incrementality testing, and the broader AdTech ecosystem, including Meta, Google, and TikTok.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Translation:&lt;/strong&gt; The rare ability to translate complex data science and Bayesian models into highly digestible commercial insights for non-technical executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to articulate complex concepts clearly and persuasively to diverse audiences. Proven track record of working effectively in cross-functional teams. Ability to build consensus and drive alignment across diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong problem-solving abilities with a proactive approach to identifying and addressing challenges. Ability to navigate ambiguity and make sound decisions under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for learning and development within the Blenheim Chalcot venture network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to our London HQ and cross-team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days PTO including 11 federal public holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your birthday off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily office snacks and treats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
